<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Athanagild</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 567</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Athanagild was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 554 to 567. He rebelled against King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agila-i">Agila I</a> and sought help from the Byzantine emperor Justinian, whose forces then seized a coastal strip of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> his residence, and his daughters <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunhilda-of-austrasia">Brunhilda</a> and Galswintha married the Frankish kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigebert-i">Sigebert I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilperic-i">Chilperic I</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Athanagild</b>'s invitation to Justinian I during the civil war of 549 brought a Byzantine province of Spania that lasted until 625.</blockquote><a href="/empire/visigothic-kingdom">Visigothic Kingdom · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In 552 the Visigothic noble <b>Athanagild</b>, rebelling against King Agila, sought help from Justinian.</blockquote><a href="/state/byzantine-spania">Byzantine Spania</a></li><li><blockquote>His successor <b>Athanagild</b> kept the autonomy for a time.</blockquote><a href="/state/tudmir">Tudmir</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Toletum, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=39.86,-4.02&amp;year=557" aria-label="Toletum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4451 737 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Athanagild"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4901 1007h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4901 1007h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=39.86,-4.02&amp;year=557">What was here in 557 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
